#!/usr/bin/env bash

##	Purpose:
##		Lets 'dogfood_shcl' be typed at a shell without anyone having to know it
##		is a pwsh script. dogfood_shcl.ps1 takes in a new build, rotates the pool
##		and prints which one to run, and this runs it in its own place, with
##		every argument but --no-update as typed. So shcl's exit code comes back,
##		after a Ctrl+C too. The same file goes in the linux/bash and macos/bash
##		util dirs; the .ps1 works out the per-platform paths itself.
##	History: At bottom of script.

